<title>USA: NYPA sees 965 MW Indian Point 3 shut thru mid-Feb.</title>
<headline>NYPA sees 965 MW Indian Point 3 shut thru mid-Feb.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The New York Power Authority (NYPA) said Friday its 965 megawatt (MW) Indian Point 3 nuclear power unit would stay shut through mid-February for replacement work in its primary containment area.</p>
<p>&quot;It'll be another three to four weeks,&quot; replied an onsite spokesman when asked about a restart schedule.</p>
<p>NYPA previously said Indian Point 3 would resume operation later this week after it was taken off line last Saturday to repair its feedwater heaters.</p>
</text>
